## Langfuse adds role-based access for trace media and storage exports

Source: Langfuse — https://langfuse.com/changelog/2026-11-06-s3-iam-role-auth
Published: 2026-11-06
Channel: news

Langfuse is an AI observability platform that displays application traces, records of an application’s operations that can include media, and supports scheduled storage exports. Its announcement adds access to Amazon S3 buckets by assuming an AWS Identity and Access Management role, avoiding the need to store long-lived access keys in Langfuse.

For scheduled exports, users configure the role through the interface or the integration endpoint with authType set to ROLE_ARN. External Media Storage can also use it to render media from a team’s own bucket inside traces. The feature requires Cloud Enterprise or self-hosted Enterprise; self-hosted deployments additionally need LANGFUSE_CROSS_ACCOUNT_ROLE_ARN configured. Access keys remain supported and are still the default.

Why it matters: Enterprise teams exporting traces or displaying private media can review role authentication as an alternative to stored long-lived keys.

